// The `int128` sub-library backs the native `i128` and `u128` types. It has no
// callable API: the types and their arithmetic are handled by the language
// engine.
//
// Under the hood it generates `core_int128.h`/`core_int128.cpp`, which
// implement `i128`/`u128` as a portable software type: each value is a pair of
// `u64` halves (lo/hi) with overloaded operators and manual arithmetic
// (carry/borrow, multi-word multiply and divide). The target toolchains (AVR
// and ARM Cortex-M) have no native `__int128`, so the codegen calls these
// helpers for every 128-bit operation.
